465","ma-c-ac721a7d8c7a91a85009","ma-c-b5b711cebf0f8b7a7507","ma-c-b8f90701e06d839795c9","ma-c-bb87ce5c769c6b8c4a75","ma-c-fd3e29df517d07e6ee7c"],"leaves":["ma-c-015ccac42c792ff9c739","ma-c-0498a9b967eec2994586","ma-c-122567974c781b77287c","ma-c-123d4e58db6fb943ee33","ma-c-15474660f8c3e18714a7","ma-c-23b2614b245f89fb4d1f","ma-c-38421cb3a01ed88ec9ad","ma-c-4165b3bb91323de70c40","ma-c-444971e0fb8d4c7eb72d","ma-c-4721261c1b1ae5e944ad","ma-c-533ae16dea6e0224c26e","ma-c-56bcb2a6092814026898","ma-c-5e8e6207aa178205bdac","ma-c-62e229a797d0362705e4","ma-c-67ee42ae2eb72a8204c0","ma-c-6941708a4d226cec1b06","ma-c-77e4298665af3bfb6995","ma-c-7ba0c6fd79b37822cbab","ma-c-9ac8095fb380d5bb5a80","ma-c-a64eb263cd002744c465","ma-c-ac721a7d8c7a91a85009","ma-c-b5b711cebf0f8b7a7507","ma-c-b8f90701e06d839795c9","ma-c-ba10c48ce07aa4701740","ma-c-bb87ce5c769c6b8c4a75","ma-c-e53b1966c488dee4885a","ma-c-fd3e29df517d07e6ee7c"],"papers":{"arXiv:0710.0810":{"abstract":"Tridiagonal canonical forms of square matrices under congruence or *congruence, pairs of symmetric or skew-symmetric matrices under congruence, and pairs of Hermitian matrices under *congruence are given over an algebraically closed field of characteristic different from 2.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1004.3590":{"abstract":"We construct the Hasse diagrams $G_2$ and $G_3$ for the closure ordering on the sets of congruence classes of $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3$ complex matrices. In other words, we construct two directed graphs whose vertices are $2\\times 2$ or, respectively, $3\\times 3$ canonical matrices under congruence and there is a directed path from $A$ to $B$ if and only if $A$ can be transformed by an arbitrari","authors":["Andrii Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Bo Kågström"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1208.5414":{"abstract":"For a given poset, we consider its representations by systems of subspaces of a unitary space ordered by inclusion. We classify such systems for all posets for which an explicit classification is possible.","authors":["Vitalij M. Bondarenko","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tatiana Klimchuk"],"year":"2012"},"arXiv:1403.2645":{"abstract":"We give a method for constructing a regularizing decomposition of a matrix pencil, which is formulated in terms of the linear mappings. We prove that two pencils are topologically equivalent if and only if their regularizing decompositions coincide up to permutation of summands and their regular parts coincide up to homeomorphisms of their spaces.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Rybalkina","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:1208.5418":{"abstract":"We give a canonical form of matrices of a cycle of linear or semilinear mapping V_1 --- V_2 --- ... --- V_t --- V_1 in which all V_i are complex vector spaces, each line is an arrow ---> or <---, and each arrow denotes a linear or semilinear mapping.","authors":["Debora Duarte de Oliveira","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tatiana Klimchuk"],"year":"2012"},"arXiv:1810.09219":{"abstract":"In representation theory, a classification problem is called wild if it contains the problem of classifying matrix pairs up to simultaneous similarity. The latter problem is considered as hopeless; it contains the problem of classifying an arbitrary finite system of vector spaces and linear mappings between them. We prove that an analogous \"universal\" problem in the theory of tensors of order at m","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Joshua A. Grochow","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:0710.0928":{"abstract":"We give canonical matrices of bilinear or sesquilinear forms UxV-->C, (V/U)xV-->C, in which V is a vector space over the field C of complex numbers and U is its subspace.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1611.04527":{"abstract":"The matrix equation $AX-XB=C$ has a solution if and only if the matrices [A&C\\\\0&B] and [A &0\\\\0 & B] are similar. This criterion was proved over a field by W.E. Roth (1952) and over the skew field of quaternions by Huang Liping (1996). H.K. Wimmer (1988) obtained an analogous criterion for the matrix equation $X-AXB=C$ over a field. We extend these criteria to the matrix equations $AX-\\widehat XB","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2016"},"arXiv:1011.0040":{"abstract":"Each square complex matrix is unitarily similar to an upper triangular matrix with diagonal entries in any prescribed order. Let A and B be upper triangular n-by-n matrices that (i) are not similar to direct sums of matrices of smaller sizes, or (ii) are in general position and have the same main diagonal. We prove that A and B are unitarily similar if and only if ||h(A_k)||=||h(B_k)|| for all com","authors":["Douglas Farenick","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tatiana G. Gerasimova"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1709.10334":{"abstract":"For each two-dimensional vector space $V$ of commuting $n\\times n$ matrices over a field $\\mathbb F$ with at least 3 elements, we denote by $\\widetilde V$ the vector space of all $(n+1)\\times(n+1)$ matrices of the form $\\left[\\begin{smallmatrix}A&*\\\\0&0\\end{smallmatrix}\\right]$ with $A\\in V$. We prove the wildness of the problem of classifying Lie algebras $\\widetilde V$ with the bracket operation","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Anatolii P. Petravchuk"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1701.08826":{"abstract":"W.Specht (1940) proved that two $n\\times n$ complex matrices $A$ and $B$ are unitarily similar if and only if $\\operatorname{trace} w(A,A^{\\ast}) = \\operatorname{trace} w(B,B^{\\ast})$ for every word $w(x,y)$ in two noncommuting variables. We extend his criterion and its generalizations by N.A.Wiegmann (1961) and N.Jing (2015) to an arbitrary system $\\mathcal A$ consisting of complex or real inner ","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2017"},"arXiv:1605.07580":{"abstract":"For an admissible affine vertex algebra $V_k(\\mathfrak{g})$ of type $A$, we describe a new family of relaxed highest weight representations of $V_k(\\mathfrak{g})$. They are simple quotients of representations of the affine Kac-Moody algebra $\\widehat{\\mathfrak{g}}$ induced from the following $\\mathfrak{g}$-modules: 1) generic Gelfand-Tsetlin modules in the principal nilpotent orbit, in particular ","authors":["Tomoyuki Arakawa","Vyacheslav Futorny","Luis Enrique Ramirez"],"year":"2016"}}}